  "notes": [
    "Example catalog:null is a report-only model fixture, not a completed production envelope. Production completed envelope has existing raw Catalog object transient only.",
    "Counts clamp to max_count; times clamp to max_time_us. Ordinals are zero-based positions, never catalog member IDs.",
    "Unknown enum strings map unknown (role maps other); unknown codes map other_native_issue; no exception text is exported.",
    "Issue array unique first-occurrence order. Summary gathers catalog, then NCA, then group issues.",
    "Digest mismatch is an observation on an untrusted embedded digest, not authentication or a corruption conclusion.",
    "OFF inspectObserved throws fixed selected_content_unavailable, preserves pending VM exceptions; no native report source built by default.",
    "Key state is parser output state, not importer line validation. Null counts mean no store was constructed; partial counts are explicit on failure. Present does not imply regular or readable. A skipped present entry was not eligible under the original FileExists decision.",
    "Title-key lookup is a read-only loaded-map probe only. Matched does not prove decryption, authorization or correct content. No Rights ID, key, hash, filename, path, raw line or exception text is retained.",
    "Container and member sizes are canonical decimal uint64 strings, not byte contents. Scope is this one scanned container only; external associations are not included. Filename content IDs are hints only, not a full hash or CNMT reference mapping.",
    "All real preview callers use full hash not_performed; not_reported is reserved for other internal caller options.",
    "The original v1 string-enum fallback applies only to original fields. New v2 enums use exactly the listed allowed sets; consumers reject unknown v2 states. counts_partial also remains true for short/unreliable reads or a failed presence probe even when the legacy parser returns successfully."
  ],
